.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/conservative-designer/input.md:78:Produce a design proposal per your role contract. Read the ACTUAL SITE first (index.html, about/, contact/, docs/, kessan/, incidents/, reports/, agent-readiness/, privacy/, llms.txt, sitemap.xml), then .agent-org/intake-template.md and .agent-org/knowledge/ui/ (cards + cited anchors). Continuity duties: the wording-FROZEN gate is mechanical and absolute — the spec must inventory which surfaces carry which text blocks so Stage B cannot orphan content; bilingual reality must be mapped from the actual pages (which are JA, which EN, which mixed); accessibility floors (contrast, focus, text alternatives) are acceptance criteria; static GitHub Pages constraints (relative paths, no build step) bind every frame/presentation decision; the spec must be implementable by codex in one Stage B cycle. Include the continuity object.
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:12:  "objective": "Ratify docs/design/uiux-spec.md for mishima-computing.github.io: a positive design-thesis, five layers instantiated for the real content, Decidable/Advisory composition propositions with per-objective thresholds, a bilingual JA/EN decision, and an explicit motion-restraint decision, under wording-FROZEN / structure-order-staging-format-FREE scope, claim-class-1 effects only.",
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:18:      "reason": "Collides with the 'no new pages' non-goal and an absent owner ruling; aufheben must not expand non-goals. Baseline is deep-linking the trust register to existing surfaces; HTML rendering is recorded in the spec as an owner-ruling-gated option only."
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:33:      "reason": "They enter the spec only as wording-preservation inventory entries; restructuring machine-facing files exceeds the UI/UX deliverable and risks the mechanical gate for zero taste-gate benefit."
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:41:  "implementation_summary": "Write docs/design/uiux-spec.md per .agent-org/intake-template.md. Sections: (1) design-thesis 'Evidence Ledger' stated as a per-view checkable proposition (each view names its proof artifact and adjacency). (2) Five layers: strategy=trust/traceability K.K. performing its own product; scope=all 9 owner-listed pages plus wording inventory covering JS-injected text, metadata, llms.txt, manifest; structure=trust register grouping with deep-link baseline and owner-gated HTML-surface option; frame=personhood-first first viewport, ledger sections, responsive table rules; presentation=per-script tokens, sober disclosure register, restrained Mishima/Fuji identity. (3) Composition propositions each marked Decidable or Advisory with objective rationale: >=1 verifiable proof artifact per index section (Decidable; metrics 100%/<10ms/24/7 explicitly excluded from the definition); <=2 consecutive same-type sections (Decidable); first-viewport = legal personhood + 1 proof artifact + 1 action (Decidable); section-rhythm variety (Advisory). (4) Bilingual: JA lead on all current views, EN visible support, measure budgets JA 15-40ch / EN 45-75ch, no JS-gated visibility; includes a pre-Stage-B verification step for block-multiset gate semantics on paired spans, with recorded fallback (both languages always-visible in DOM). (5) Motion-restraint decision with proves:/timing-ranges table, reduced-motion removal, WCAG SC 2.2.2/2.3.1/2.3.3 acceptance entries. All effect claims limited to claim-class-1 (credibility, focus, scanability, legibility, appeal).",
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:51:    "Spec contains a wording-preservation inventory covering HTML body text, JS-injected UI text, metadata, llms.txt, sitemap labels, and manifest text.",
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:53:    "The trust-register structure specifies deep-link baseline for incidents/docs markdown and marks any HTML surfacing as gated on an explicit owner ruling, without expanding non-goals.",
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:78:    "CI constraints incomplete: no CI action writer outputs or gap reports were provided to this synthesis; the existing block-multiset wording gate is owner-declared and applies to Stage B, not Stage A. Do not invent additional CI gates."
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:84:    "Spec must require all content remain readable without JavaScript execution (no JS-gated visibility), per the hard constraint and ADR-0001 rationale."
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:100:    "Perceptual-gate tooling (#44).",
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:104:    "Owner taste gate is subjective; if つまらない meant insufficient visual spectacle, a sober evidence ledger could fail again. Mitigation: thesis mandates boldness via proof density and section-type variety, and carries Mishima/Fuji identity in presentation, not austerity.",
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:106:    "Block-multiset gate semantics on paired JA/EN spans and JS-injected text are unverified; bilingual restructuring could trip the mechanical gate. Mitigation: pre-Stage-B gate dry-run required; fallback keeps both languages always-visible in DOM.",
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:108:    "Removing ambient motion and demoting the hero changes the brand energy the owner may currently like; mitigated by marking each structural bet separable with a recorded fallback.",
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:111:  "fallback_plan": "Stage A is git-revertible: replace or delete docs/design/uiux-spec.md before merge. Inside the spec, three structural bets are separable with recorded fallbacks: (1) bilingual model falls back to both-languages-always-visible without the JS toggle if gate semantics fail verification; (2) trust register falls back to deep-linking existing surfaces if HTML surfacing is ruled a new page; (3) if first-viewport restructuring is contested, the minimum viable thesis is per-view proof-artifact adjacency alone (aggressive H1 core), which still satisfies the design-thesis requirement.",
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:112:  "handoff_to_implementer": "Write docs/design/uiux-spec.md exactly per implementation_summary and acceptance_criteria. Touch no other file. Quote frozen text blocks verbatim when referencing them; never paraphrase content into the spec as replacement wording. Mark every composition proposition Decidable or Advisory with threshold, rationale, and Stage B verification artifact. Record the motion-restraint and bilingual decisions as explicit decisions with fallbacks, citing anchors (anchor:motion#nng-animation-duration, anchor:accessibility, anchor:color, ui-* profile cards). Cite tailscale/deepseek-/en exemplars as fetch-verified only; antgroup may appear solely as hypothesis-class. Do not claim adoption or completion; ratification occurs by merge."
.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/codex/implementer/prompt.txt:121:Implement exactly per contract: Stage A is DOCS-ONLY (docs/design/uiux-spec.md and any contract-listed gate-spec docs). Read the actual site pages while writing the wording inventory — every text block must be inventoried from the real HTML. Run required_checks. If a sandbox write is denied, author the content to the run directory for controller transcription.
.agent-runs/20260612-123650-benchmark-stage-b/carriers/codex/implementer/fixup5-prompt.txt:8:A) LEAD-EMPHASIS SWITCH (preferred if clean): the button becomes a lead-language preference. html[lang=en] swaps visual emphasis via CSS only — .lang-en becomes lead-prominent (size/weight/order) and .lang-ja becomes support — BOTH always visible in DOM (the spec's invariant). Button labels EN/JA and aria labels keep their existing strings (wording gate stays green). Works without JS on first paint (default JA-lead).
.agent-runs/20260612-123650-benchmark-stage-b/carriers/codex/implementer/fixup5-prompt.txt:10:B) REMOVAL: delete the button, its JS, and its CSS. The owner's message authorizes the wording deletion of the EN/JA labels + aria strings (record this authorization in your notes and list the removed strings).
