.agent-runs/20260612-121929-benchmark-stage-a/carriers/claude/aufheben-designer/cli-output.json:1:{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":96981,"duration_api_ms":98763,"ttft_ms":11592,"ttft_stream_ms":3982,"time_to_request_ms":27,"num_turns":3,"result":"Both designer inputs declare `overall_posture: grounded` with usable evidence pointers on every grounded claim; genius hypotheses H1–H3 are `confirmed` with repo and fetch-verified external refs. The declared conflict_points are high-confidence disagreement inputs, but all four major conflicts (docs/incidents surface scope, hero demotion, JS language toggle, motion restraint) converge on the same resolution across all three inputs or admit a recorded in-spec fallback, and the Stage A artifact is a docs-only, git-revertible merge. Completeness × reversibility supports **proceed**; speculative claims (owner-taste reading, gate semantics on paired spans) are downgraded and handled as gated decisions inside the contract rather than assumed.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"role_id\": \"aufheben-designer\",\n  \"contract_id\": \"IC-20260612-stageA-uiux-spec-001\",\n  \"objective\": \"Ratify docs/design/uiux-spec.md for mishima-computing.github.io: a positive design-thesis, five layers instantiated for the real content, Decidable/Advisory composition propositions with per-objective thresholds, a bilingual JA/EN decision, and an explicit motion-restraint decision, under wording-FROZEN / structure-order-staging-format-FREE scope, claim-class-1 effects only.\",\n  \"selected_direction\": \"Synthesis of aggressive H1 + conservative Trust Ledger + genius H1-H3. Design-thesis: 'Evidence Ledger — the company performs its own trust product on itself.' Every index-level view pairs frozen text with an adjacent verifiable proof artifact (kessan notice, incident post-mortem, ADR-0001, agent-readiness manifest, GitHub provenance, serverless contact demo). First viewport = company personhood (JA legal name + registered facts) plus exactly one proof artifact; unverifiable hero metrics survive verbatim but stage below the fold and are excluded from the proof-artifact definition. JA is lead language per view with EN as visible support, per-script tokens (JA ~15-40ch, EN ~45-75ch measure budgets), no JS dependency for content visibility. Motion restraint is an explicit recorded decision: opacity/transform only, NN/g duration bands cited (no fixed ms constants), prefers-reduced-motion removes all motion, ambient grid-bg/glow-orb/pulse made static or removed with WCAG 2.2.2/2.3.1/2.3.3 audit noted.\",\n  \"rejected_parts\": [\n    {\n      \"source\": \"aggressive-designer\",\n      \"rejected_part\": \"H3 default form: promoting incidents/ and docs/ markdown into new HTML surfaces and regrouping primary nav around them as the baseline structure.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Collides with the 'no new pages' non-goal and an absent owner ruling; aufheben must not expand non-goals. Baseline is deep-linking the trust register to existing surfaces; HTML rendering is recorded in the spec as an owner-ruling-gated option only.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"aggressive-designer\",\n      \"rejected_part\": \"Assumption that the current live site is the previously failed attempt and therefore direct evidence of rejected owner taste.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Listed only under assumptions with no evidence pointer; downgraded to speculative per role policy. The spec must justify staging via genre/profile evidence, not via inferred owner-taste history.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"conservative-designer\",\n      \"rejected_part\": \"Fixed motion constant 'motion off or 150-300ms state proof only' in handoff_notes.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Genius H3 and ui-feel-foundations require cited duration bands with rationale, never inherited fixed ms constants; the spec cites anchor:motion#nng-animation-duration bands plus proves:/timing-ranges discipline instead.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"conservative-designer\",\n      \"rejected_part\": \"Treating llms.txt, sitemap.xml, manifest.json, and robots.txt as design surfaces the spec restructures.\",\n      \"reason\": \"They enter the spec only as wording-preservation inventory entries; restructuring machine-facing files exceeds the UI/UX deliverable and risks the mechanical gate for zero taste-gate benefit.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"source\": \"genius\",\n      \"rejected_part\": \"Importing Vanta/Drata surface patterns (badge walls, customer counts) beyond genre confirmation; antgroup as citable exemplar; the empty fourth hypothesis stub.\",\n      \"reason\": \"Wording is frozen and the company holds no certifications, so badge/count patterns are uncopyable; antgroup is hypothesis-class unverified-by-fetch; the empty stub is a mechanical artifact carrying no content.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"implementation_summary\": \"Write docs/design/uiux-spec.md per .agent-org/intake-template.md. Sections: (1) design-thesis 'Evidence Ledger' stated as a per-view checkable proposition (each view names its proof artifact and adjacency). (2) Five layers: strategy=trust/traceability K.K. performing its own product; scope=all 9 owner-listed pages plus wording inventory covering JS-injected text, metadata, llms.txt, manifest; structure=trust register grouping with deep-link baseline and owner-gated HTML-surface option; frame=personhood-first first viewport, ledger sections, responsive table rules; presentation=per-script tokens, sober disclosure register, restrained Mishima/Fuji identity. (3) Composition propositions each marked Decidable or Advisory with objective rationale: >=1 verifiable proof artifact per index section (Decidable; metrics 100%/<10ms/24/7 explicitly excluded from the definition); <=2 consecutive same-type sections (Decidable); first-viewport = legal personhood + 1 proof artifact + 1 action (Decidable); section-rhythm variety (Advisory). (4) Bilingual: JA lead on all current views, EN visible support, measure budgets JA 15-40ch / EN 45-75ch, no JS-gated visibility; includes a pre-Stage-B verification step for block-multiset gate semantics on paired spans, with recorded fallback (both languages always-visible in DOM). (5) Motion-restraint decision with proves:/timing-ranges table, reduced-motion removal, WCAG SC 2.2.2/2.3.1/2.3.3 acceptance entries. All effect claims limited to claim-class-1 (credibility, focus, scanability, legibility, appeal).\",\n  \"acceptance_criteria\": [\n    \"docs/design/uiux-spec.md exists, follows .agent-org/intake-template.md, and is the only file changed in the Stage A diff.\",\n    \"The design-thesis names a positive memorable move checkable per view; no section of the spec is prohibition-only.\",\n    \"All five layers are instantiated with this site's actual pages and content blocks, not generic guidance.\",\n    \"Every composition proposition is marked Decidable or Advisory, carries a threshold with an objective-derived rationale, and names its Stage B verification artifact.\",\n    \"Proof-artifact definition explicitly excludes the frozen unverifiable metric blocks; those blocks are staged verbatim below the first viewport.\",\n    \"Lead language is declared per view (JA lead, EN visible support) with per-script tokens and measure budgets; spec states no content visibility may depend on JS.\",\n    \"Motion section records an explicit decision: opacity/transform only, NN/g band citations without fixed ms constants, prefers-reduced-motion removes all motion, existing ambient animations resolved (static or removed).\",\n    \"WCAG 2.2 floors (4.5:1 body / 3:1 large-text and non-text contrast, focus visibility, SC 2.2.2/2.3.1/2.3.3) appear as non-negotiable acceptance criteria, not advisory notes.\",\n    \"Spec contains a wording-preservation inventory covering HTML body text, JS-injected UI text, metadata, llms.txt, sitemap labels, and manifest text.\",\n    \"All claimed effects are claim-class-1 per anchor:evaluation-instruments#claim-classes; no conversion/engagement/SEO claims appear.\",\n    \"The trust-register structure specifies deep-link baseline for incidents/docs markdown and marks any HTML surfacing as gated on an explicit owner ruling, without expanding non-goals.\",\n    \"The spec marks its three structural bets (hero demotion, bilingual model, register grouping) as separable decisions each with a recorded fallback.\"\n  ],\n  \"files_allowed_to_change\": [\n    \"docs/design/uiux-spec.md\"\n  ],\n  \"files_not_allowed_to_change\": [\n    \"index.html\",\n    \"about/**\",\n    \"contact/**\",\n    \"privacy/**\",\n    \"kessan/**\",\n    \"incidents/**\",\n    \"reports/**\",\n    \"agent-readiness/**\",\n    \"assets/**\",\n    \"scripts/**\",\n    \".github/**\",\n    \"llms.txt\"\n  ],\n  \"required_checks\": [\n    \"Diff check: Stage A changeset touches only docs/design/uiux-spec.md (docs-only constraint).\",\n    \"Template conformance review against .agent-org/intake-template.md before merge.\",\n    \"Claim-class audit: grep spec for class-2 vocabulary (conversion, engagement, SEO, ranking) and reject if present.\",\n    \"Threshold audit: every Decidable proposition has threshold + rationale + named Stage B verification artifact.\",\n    \"CI constraints incomplete: no CI action writer outputs or gap reports were provided to this synthesis; the existing block-multiset wording gate is owner-declared and applies to Stage B, not Stage A. Do not invent additional CI gates.\"\n  ],\n  \"security_requirements\": [\n    \"No secrets, tokens, or personal data in the spec; contact-form discussion references existing serverless catalog only.\",\n    \"No new external script, font, or asset dependencies may be mandated by the spec; GitHub Pages static-hosting trust boundary unchanged.\",\n    \"Spec must not instruct Stage B to add analytics, tracking, or third-party embeds.\",\n    \"Spec must require all content remain readable without JavaScript execution (no JS-gated visibility), per the hard constraint and ADR-0001 rationale.\"\n  ],\n  \"nonfunctional_requirements\": [\n    \"WCAG 2.2 AA floors as binding acceptance criteria: contrast 4.5:1 body / 3:1 large and non-text, visible focus, keyboard operability, alt text.\",\n    \"Motion: SC 2.2.2/2.3.1/2.3.3 compliance; prefers-reduced-motion removes all animation; durations cited as NN/g bands only.\",\n    \"Typography: per-script tokens with JA ~15-40ch and EN ~45-75ch measure budgets; JLREQ/CLREQ mixed-script rules per anchor:typography-cjk-latin.\",\n    \"Static delivery: plain HTML/CSS on GitHub Pages, no build framework, no SSG; spec must be implementable with hand-edited files per ADR-0001.\",\n    \"UTF-8 no-BOM file handling discipline noted for Stage B, per the published mojibake incident.\",\n    \"Spec must keep Stage B mechanically self-checkable before the single owner presentation (each Decidable check names its artifact).\"\n  ],\n  \"non_goals\": [\n    \"Stage B implementation (no HTML/CSS/JS edits in Stage A).\",\n    \"Content rewriting, translation, summarizing, merging, or dropping any text block.\",\n    \"New public pages (HTML surfacing of incidents/docs markdown only if a future explicit owner ruling permits; the spec must not presume it).\",\n    \"Analytics, CMS, build frameworks, or package managers.\",\n    \"Changes to scripts/ or CI workflows.\",\n    \"Perceptual-gate tooling (#44).\",\n    \"Claim-class-2 effect claims anywhere in the spec.\"\n  ],\n  \"risks\": [\n    \"Owner taste gate is subjective; if つまらない meant insufficient visual spectacle, a sober evidence ledger could fail again. Mitigation: thesis mandates boldness via proof density and section-type variety, and carries Mishima/Fuji identity in presentation, not austerity.\",\n    \"Proof inventory is thin (kessan 準備中, one incident); per-view artifact floors could force padding. Mitigation: spec frames candor staging ('scheduled', capital ¥10,000) as deliberate transparency and sets the floor per index section, not per page.\",\n    \"Block-multiset gate semantics on paired JA/EN spans and JS-injected text are unverified; bilingual restructuring could trip the mechanical gate. Mitigation: pre-Stage-B gate dry-run required; fallback keeps both languages always-visible in DOM.\",\n    \"Dark glow palette may fail worst-case-region 4.5:1 audits, forcing larger presentation changes than estimated; spec must declare contrast floors as binding so Stage B budgets for it.\",\n    \"Removing ambient motion and demoting the hero changes the brand energy the owner may currently like; mitigated by marking each structural bet separable with a recorded fallback.\",\n    \"Deep-link-only trust register (if HTML surfacing stays disallowed) weakens on-site proof density; floors must be satisfiable with existing HTML surfaces alone.\"\n  ],\n  \"fallback_plan\": \"Stage A is git-revertible: replace or delete docs/design/uiux-spec.md before merge. Inside the spec, three structural bets are separable with recorded fallbacks: (1) bilingual model falls back to both-languages-always-visible without the JS toggle if gate semantics fail verification; (2) trust register falls back to deep-linking existing surfaces if HTML surfacing is ruled a new page; (3) if first-viewport restructuring is contested, the minimum viable thesis is per-view proof-artifact adjacency alone (aggressive H1 core), which still satisfies the design-thesis requirement.\",\n  \"handoff_to_implementer\": \"Write docs/design/uiux-spec.md exactly per implementation_summary and acceptance_criteria. Touch no other file. Quote frozen text blocks verbatim when referencing them; never paraphrase content into the spec as replacement wording. Mark every composition proposition Decidable or Advisory with threshold, rationale, and Stage B verification artifact. Record the motion-restraint and bilingual decisions as explicit decisions with fallbacks, citing anchors (anchor:motion#nng-animation-duration, anchor:accessibility, anchor:color, ui-* profile cards). Cite tailscale/deepseek-/en exemplars as fetch-verified only; antgroup may appear solely as hypothesis-class. Do not claim adoption or completion; ratification occurs by merge.\"\n}\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"7c62ed85-d92d-4f38-bd92-e52c2c01b75a","total_cost_usd":0.8866510000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":1779,"cache_creation_input_tokens":23639,"cache_read_input_tokens":23252,"output_tokens":7194,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":23639,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":6465,"cache_read_input_tokens":20841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5209,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5209},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":13029,"outputTokens":20,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.013129,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-fable-5[1m]":{"inputTokens":1779,"outputTokens":7194,"cacheReadInputTokens":23252,"cacheCreationInputTokens":23639,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.873522,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"0761afc9-bd73-4f98-8334-cd6c306733b6"}
